From 01ed4e6363350323b13d99c47e18b4cb8e1d8fc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:19:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: ROME: reset after changing the address

A QCA6174 (ROME) without a valid address comes up unconfigured. When
userspace sets the public address, the controller runs its setup again
(non-persistent setup: rampatch, NVM, HCI reset) and qca_set_bdaddr_rome()
writes the address tag. On the ZTE Axon 7 the HCI reset of the init that
follows timed out on about one boot in five ("Opcode 0x0c03 failed:
-110") and hci0 stayed in setup until the driver was rebound.

Send an HCI reset right after the address tag was written and wait for
its answer (1 s, up to 5 tries) before init goes on. With it, 16 of 16
boots came up without a timeout (before: 6 failures in 28 boots); the
first reset always answered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i49UMoL3MhGT7nwMzG
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
index 22b08ab05..d82f8070f 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@ int qca_set_bdaddr_rome(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr)
 {
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 	u8 cmd[9];
-	int err;
+	int err, i;
 
 	cmd[0] = EDL_NVM_ACCESS_SET_REQ_CMD;
 	cmd[1] = 0x02; 			/* TAG ID */
@@ -676,6 +676,25 @@ int qca_set_bdaddr_rome(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr)
 
 	kfree_skb(skb);
 
+	/*
+	 * ROME restarts after the address tag changed. The HCI reset of the
+	 * following init sometimes arrived while it did and timed out ("Opcode
+	 * 0x0c03 failed: -110"), leaving the controller in setup for good.
+	 * Wait until it answers a reset again.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+		skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, HCI_OP_RESET, 0, NULL,
+				     msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
+		if (!IS_ERR(skb)) {
+			kfree_skb(skb);
+			if (i)
+				bt_dev_info(hdev, "QCA reset after the address change: %d tries",
+					    i + 1);
+			return 0;
+		}
+	}
+	bt_dev_warn(hdev, "QCA no reset answer after the address change");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qca_set_bdaddr_rome);
